Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: restore BPI-R4 2.5G PHY LED pinctrl

The 24.10 board baseline defines pinctrl groups in the shared BPI-R4 DTSI
instead of including mt7988a-pinctrl.dtsi. Keep the internal 2.5G PHY LED
group there as well: the existing 2g5 and PoE variants both reference it.
Without it, even a standard R4 kernel build fails in the full dtbs target.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4.dtsi
@@ -518,6 +518,13 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	i2p5gbe_led0_pins: 2p5gbe-led0-pins {
+		mux {
+			function = "led";
+			groups = "2p5gbe_led0";
+		};
+	};
+
 	pwm0_pins: pwm0-pins {
 		mux {
 			groups = "pwm0";
